! Four hydrogen atoms in a chain, one species, noncollinear and ferromagnetic,
! with symmetry left ON.
!
! The point of the cell is that its group is large -- 16 operations, reducing a
! 2x2x4 grid to 9 k-points -- so replacing its moments with a texture visibly
! changes both numbers. It is the demonstration cell for `with_moments`: a
! cycloid on these four sites drops the group to 4 and the k-set grows to 12.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.66666666666667,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 1, ecutwfc = 20.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.00
 H 0.0 0.0 0.25
 H 0.0 0.0 0.50
 H 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS {automatic}
 2 2 4 0 0 0
